WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:04.360
How should the US government and the rest of us respond to the Coronavirus,

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:09.160
which has just been declared a global pandemic by the World Health Organization.

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:14.940
Balaji Srinivasan, who was on the short list to head up Donald Trump's Food and Drug Administration,

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:16.780
has some strong opinions.

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:21.780
He's a former venture capitalist at Andreessen Horowitz, and he's a serial entrepreneur

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:27.420
with a Phd in electrical engineering. The genetic testing company he cofounded, Counsyl,

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:34.280
helped change the way millions of people prepare for parenthood, and his cryptocurrency startup, Earn.com,

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:38.560
was acquired by Coinbase, where he served as chief technology officer.

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:43.980
In a prescient, lively, and constantly updated Twitter feed, Srinivasan has been way ahead of the curve

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:49.560
in noting the Coronavirus's spread, and potential to cause a global public health crisis,

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:54.000
and a massive economic and social disruption to life as we know it.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.060
Balaji, thanks for talking. Hello.

00:00:57.060 --> 00:01:02.820
Let's get right to it, you were really early
in sounding the alarm about Coronavirus,

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:06.920
how did you hear about it and why were you on top of it,

00:01:06.920 --> 00:52:14.700
and what does that say about Silicon Valley versus journalists on the east coast?

